# Citation metadata for rAPIdtools. GitHub reads this file to show the
# "Cite this repository" button; Zenodo reads it when archiving a release.
# Keep `version` and `date-released` in step with pyproject.toml and CHANGELOG.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rAPIdtools in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "rAPIdtools: AI inference and localization for post-disaster geospatial datasets"
abstract: >-
  rAPIdtools is a Python toolkit that connects post-disaster orthomosaics,
  basemaps and street-level imagery with vision-language models. It crops
  imagery around every physical asset visible in imagery, runs the crops
  through hosted or local models, discovers and regularizes asset geometries
  with SAM 3, and writes the results back to GeoJSON or Shapefile.
authors:
  - family-names: Cetiner
    given-names: Barbaros
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9726-8120"
    affiliation: "RAPID Facility, University of Washington"
  - name: "RAPID Facility"
    website: "https://www.uwrapid.org/"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/RAPID-Facility/rAPIdtools"
url: "https://rapid-facility.github.io/rAPIdtools/"
keywords:
  - natural hazards
  - damage assessment
  - post-disaster reconnaissance
  - remote sensing
  - aerial imagery
  - street-level imagery
  - vision-language models
  - computer vision
  - GIS
